// # fs — Filesystem + Host OS (mirrors std/fs)
//
// Logline: The host surface — OS syscalls (sys_exec, sys_args), the policy getenv filter, file I/O, the net-floor loopback constraint, the host process info, the rlimit setter, the time+rand source, the loopback-only DNS resolver, and the print family.
//
// Setup: os/ is the syscall-level surface. All operations are cap-gated: ProcessCap for sys_exec, FsCap for file I/O, NetCap for netfloor/dns, EnvCap for getenv. The DNS resolver refuses to call getaddrinfo (which would walk /etc/hosts and upstream DNS, defeating the net-floor loopback constraint).
//
// Beats:
//   1. os/sys.c — sys_exec, sys_args, policy getenv (OODA_/OO_ keys only).
//   2. os/fs.c — file I/O with cap-gated path safety.
//   3. os/netfloor.c — net-floor loopback constraint (no unrestricted resolver).
//   4. os/host.c — host process info (pid, ppid, etc.).
//   5. os/dns.c — the loopback-only DNS resolver (the security-relevant policy point).
//   6. os/rlimit.c — setrlimit wrapper (RLIMIT_AS, RLIMIT_NOFILE, RLIMIT_CPU).
//   7. os/time_rand.c — monotonic time + secure random.
//   8. io/print.c — stdout/stderr print family (no cap-gate in v1.0.1).
//
// ──▓▓ fs ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: fail-closed: no getaddrinfo, no unrestricted env ::
